<div class="d-flex align-items-center mb-3">
  <h2 class="h4 mb-0 fw-semibold">
    <i class="fa-solid fa-table-columns me-2 text-primary"></i>Several tables
  </h2>
  <span class="badge bg-light text-dark border ms-3">isolation du loader</span>
</div>
<p class="text-muted mb-4">
  Deux éléments portent <code>data-toggle=datatable</code>. Le premier est volontairement
  incomplet — un <code>&lt;table&gt;</code> marqué mais sans attribut
  <code>data-dtf-loader</code>, ce que produit un copier-coller ou un partiel rendu hors de son
  helper. Le second est valide et doit se charger malgré lui.
</p>

<%# Deliberately hand-written, and deliberately first: render_datatable could
    never emit this. It is the shape a stray tagged element takes in a real
    application, and it is what makes Loader.load_datatables throw. %>
<table id="broken-datatable" data-toggle="datatable" class="d-none"></table>

<div class="card feature-card">
  <div class="card-body p-4">
    <%
      dt = bootstrap_datatables_for(
        :basic,
        source: api_basic_datatable_path,
        serverSide: true,
        stateSave: false,
        order: [[0, 'asc']],
      ) do |dt|
        dt.head_for :first_name, label: 'First name'
        dt.head_for :last_name,  label: 'Last name'
        dt.head_for :email,      label: 'Email'
      end
    %>
    <%= dt.render_datatable %>
  </div>
</div>
